{"title":"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 4","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Motivating_solution)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Motivating solution)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(Similar_to_3)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (Similar to 3)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c649ac774ef8194af0a27fd246c9cfcc670a3a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_i| &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c8fda85b509471f117cb6e73b2680da394de5fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$i = 1, 2, \\dots, n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"107\" height=\"16\" />.  Suppose further that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/0/e/30e11f702869122537b612b6adbe5331dd41d521.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_1| + |x_2| + \\dots + |x_n| = 19 + |x_1 + x_2 + \\dots + x_n|.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"394\" height=\"18\" />\nWhat is the smallest possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/6/8c649ac774ef8194af0a27fd246c9cfcc670a3a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_i| &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> then\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c7c53b12e318497f61229adebb8de89eecc87d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|x_1| + |x_2| + \\dots + |x_n| = 19 + |x_1 + x_2 + \\dots + x_n| &lt; n.\\]\" width=\"427\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>So <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/d/3cd94b2f473dacb68bc5efb29c7a267dc19f0944.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\ge 20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"52\" height=\"15\" />. We now just need to find an example where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/6/fb6a07a7c20f6b35462de06a47e8672ea360ca79.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 20$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />: suppose <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/b/debc06a781a21c2857e48c13bcdbf4b0fbc49e61.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k-1} = \\frac{19}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/1/1b18483f92acece035376bbe79c14341619b7c55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_{2k} = -\\frac{19}{20}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"84\" height=\"37\" />; then on the left hand side we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/4083713b0f7159a6d74a9b3b04a9c7466f0606b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\left|\\frac{19}{20}\\right| + \\left|-\\frac{19}{20}\\right| + \\dots + \\left|-\\frac{19}{20}\\right| = 20\\left(\\frac{19}{20}\\right) = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"353\" height=\"43\" />. On the right hand side, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/f/1/2f10848a105f3e65e7787b3ac57c078724766f6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$19 + \\left|\\frac{19}{20} - \\frac{19}{20} + \\dots - \\frac{19}{20}\\right| = 19 + 0 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"322\" height=\"43\" />, and so the equation can hold for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/b/9ebdac6b37bfead66bcc6ff69cc6c4cdca3a2cc9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"74\" height=\"23\" />.\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Motivating_solution.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Motivating_solution)\">Solution 2 (Motivating solution)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Motivating solution)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First off, one can test <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/b/8abc7b2e885661cb2bf301c4dff3f1897a800cdd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,-1,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"56\" height=\"15\" /> and find that the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c924be2d96aaeaadfdfd4b35b06d2a60edb5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the RHS is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> Similarly testing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/2/c/d2c8d49b1973dbf8a24e06b33eade8654645c212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,-1,-1,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"88\" height=\"15\" /> yields <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the LHS and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/c/1/bc1f9d9bf8a1b606a4188b5ce9a2af1809e27a89.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> on the RHS. It seems for every negative we gain twice of that negative on the LHS. However, when we test something like <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/7/09764ec424f03924dd836616892661fe28e02d42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1,-1,-1,-1,1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"119\" height=\"15\" /> we find the LHS to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and the RHS to be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdd1b53e5faf7a118222e4b7571d1e9afa0cf56.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> What happened? There were more negatives than positives. Why does this mean that the LHS doesn't grow? There aren't enough positives to \"cancel out!\" Therefore if for every negative we need a positive for it to cancel out to grow. We can make the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/c/17c924be2d96aaeaadfdfd4b35b06d2a60edb5d9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LHS$\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> grow by approximately <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> every time we choose a negative and a positive, so if we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/8/3/f8366cd6196dd8a9da6d38a3e9eafb109e99d53e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$20$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> numbers, namely <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> positive and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/6/fc606f7f1e530731ab4f1cc364c01dc64a4455ee.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> negative we can obtain the desired answer.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Straight off, we notice that the RHS must be greater than or equal to 19, because an absolute value only gives nonnegative values. It then becomes clear that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/0/4e085b25978e9cb40556f1ae40f84b435affe90a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_1|+|x_2|+...+|x_n|\\ge19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"211\" height=\"20\" />. If each <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195db3e04ee69d85a0aeaedbb1cf9afa97ff4546.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> were equal to 1, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/a/1ba21440957dd537f17834562b567ea84248f4c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=19$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />. However, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/a/6/9a6581e56775780f839e61d015c0668f4b6166e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_n&lt;1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"55\" height=\"17\" />, so there must be at least one extra term to satisfy the inequality. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/6479f0d1bc444e2f909d1c4c33edea74e7583187.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\boxed{020}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"76\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_4_.28Similar_to_3.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(Similar_to_3)\">Solution 4 (Similar to 3)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (Similar to 3)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Note as long as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12bb9d6a4cd412e86555d0d0030959b09861529b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> then we can set two terms <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/1/03126ea3f6549f56beb8cfc9efebe4c3a71f426e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i, x_j$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" /> as opposites on the number line and the result follows. That then implies for all even <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/c/2dcbac583f4d2fef89b5a15822fee57e4e0478db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$|x_1+\\dots+x_n| + 19 = 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"198\" height=\"20\" /> hence <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/3/633a2c173b7054a82cf4dd321c61ef426a6446a9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sum |x_i| \\geq 19$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"99\" height=\"31\" />. Equality holds if all <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/7/6c75eb8978ee0840709244e93e95693ba1825888.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" /> but we have the property <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12bb9d6a4cd412e86555d0d0030959b09861529b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i &lt; 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"51\" height=\"17\" />. So, we must account for this with one more term <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/b/67bc6daa9d6b964201d6cef60cbeb1ac5fd26ead.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x_i$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"15\" height=\"10\" /> making <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/e/e2ee1b8d89684727ca645175a7bf8b4a38ba8ed4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = \\boxed{20} \\quad \\square$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"97\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~Pinotation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_4&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle_Inequality\" title=\"Triangle Inequality\">Triangle Inequality</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME\" title=\"1988 AIME\">1988 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1988 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1988\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1988_AIME_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"1988 AIME Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AIME_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AIME Problems and Solutions\"> All AIME Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016210043\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.038 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.057 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 292/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1766/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 88/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 7727/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.660      1 -total\n 61.38%    8.384      1 Template:AIME_box\n 37.02%    5.057      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:2844:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016210043 and revision id 286663. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}